{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And the flock grew hot.</b> It did not bother to use the masculine form for the plural, as in 'if the daughters of Shiloh come out.'" "<b>Unto the rods.</b> Like 'from the rods.' 'To break <b>אל</b> Joseph <b>מן</b> Joseph.' Another interpretation: for the sake of the rods, like 'when I go down <b>אל</b> my sons.'" "<b>And the flock brought forth streaked.</b> From here on he did not set up rods; rather, the ewes that were streaked and spotted — Jacob separated and put the rest of the flock toward those that were streaked, and all the brown that belonged to Laban's flock."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:51.477550765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}